\pard\sl360\slmult1 Abstract\par

\pard\li284\sl240\slmult1 This document describes the commonly used base 64, base 32, and base 16 encoding schemes. It also discusses the use of line-feeds in encoded data, use of padding in encoded data, use of non-alphaber characters in encoded data, use of different encoding alphabets, and canonical encodings.\par
\par

