\pard\li284\sl240\slmult1\lang1049 Special processing is performed if fewer than 24 bits are available at the end of the data being encoded. A full encoding quantum is always completed at the end of a quantity. When fewer than 24 input bits are available in at input group, bits with value zero are added (on the right) to form an intergral number of 6-bit groups. Padding at the end of the data is performed using the '=' character. Since all base 64 input is an integral number of octets, only the following cases can arise :\par

\pard\fi-284\li568\sl240\slmult1 (1) The final quantum of encoding input is an integral multiple of 24 bits; here, the final unit of encoded output will be an integral multiple of 4 characters with no "=" padding.\par
(2) The final quantum of encoding input is exactly 8 bits; here, the final unit of encoded output will be two characters followed by two "=" padding characters.\par
(3) The final quantum of encoding input is exactly 16 bits; here, the final unit of encoded output will be three characters followerd by one "=" padding character.\par
